<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umar ibn al-Khattab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">caliph <a href="/years/634">634</a>–644 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Umar ibn al-Khattab was the second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>, ruling from 634 to 644 CE. Under his leadership Muslim armies conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, and he established key institutions such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diwan">diwan</a> for paying soldiers and garrison cities. He was assassinated in 644, and accounts of the Rashidun Caliphate treat his reign as central to the caliphate's foundation and governance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/umar-ibn-al-khattab.jpg" alt="Umar ibn al-Khattab" width="320" height="334" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Neuheisel from DC, US [cropped by Fazoffic] · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hagia_Sopia_6163502494_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Abu Bakr died of illness in 634 CE and was succeeded by <b>Umar ibn al-Khattab</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=21.42,39.83&amp;year=640" aria-label="Mecca on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5620 1372 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Umar ibn al-Khattab"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6070 1642h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6070 1642h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=21.42,39.83&amp;year=640">What was here in 640 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
